{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Azure Resource Group.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Azure Resource Group.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"azure resource group azure resource group","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Azure Resource Group.md","fileName":"Azure Resource Group.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Azure Resource Group","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 20:52\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Cloud Application Deployment]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Application Deployment","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","aspnetcore3andreact.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Azure Resource Group.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Azure Resource Group.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"azure resource group azure resource group","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Azure Resource Group.md","fileName":"Azure Resource Group.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Azure Resource Group","heading":"Azure Resource Group","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An Azure resource group is a management container for related cloud resources. The book places the application's App Services, service plan, and SQL resources into a shared group so they can be viewed and managed as one deployed system.\n\nThe group provides an operational boundary rather than an application runtime. Naming and environment separation should make it clear which resources belong together and which lifecycle they share.\n\nThe Azure projects group databases, applications, monitoring tools, and related services by shared purpose and lifetime. Because deleting a group removes its contained resources, it also becomes a practical cleanup boundary for temporary project infrastructure.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Application Deployment","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","as